id: ops-q6ki
title: Raise pm-ops enforced source coverage to 100/100/100/100
description: "The current fail-closed coverage gate is real but ratcheted only to 94% lines, 78% branches, and 95% functions; the verified full gate reports 94.32/78.45/95.04. Production readiness requires complete statement, branch, function, and line coverage without ignore directives, generated fixtures, or tests that merely execute code without asserting behavior."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T10:20:09.627Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T14:46:33.581Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-07T14:46:33.567Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-07T14:46:33.567Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "Coverage configuration enforces 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines; All source reaches 100/100/100/100 through meaningful unit, integration, installed-CLI, and failure-path assertions; Negative controls prove each threshold cannot be bypassed by missing reports, omitted source files, ignore comments, or changed reporter output"
definition_of_ready: Use c8 source reports to map each uncovered branch to a behavioral requirement; reject coverage ignore comments and synthetic assertions.
value: "Make every source behavior observable and regression-protected across supported CLI, SDK, platform, and failure paths."
impact: "Prevents untested error recovery, output routing, platform branches, and parser edge cases from shipping across fleet automation."
outcome: "The coverage gate fails below 100% for statements, branches, functions, or lines, and the complete behavioral suite meets all four thresholds."
why_now: "The fleet-wide mandate is 100/100/100/100, while the current verified gate is materially below it and must not be represented as complete."
risk: high
confidence: medium
resolution: "Replaced the three-metric gate with c8 four-metric enforcement, included executable scripts in source discovery, converted the remaining JavaScript hook to TypeScript, and added behavior-driven positive and negative controls."
expected_result: "Every executable source file is presence-checked and meets independently enforced 100% statement, branch, function, and line coverage."
actual_result: "Five executable TypeScript files are reported at 100/100/100/100 across 162 tests, with no coverage ignores and fail-closed negative controls."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T13:40:50.697Z","harness:codex","2026-08-07 characterization on clean main 9f755d1 with Node v22.19.0: npm ci reported zero vulnerabilities; npm run coverage passed 121 tests with 2 opt-in real-data skips and measured only index.ts/docstrings.ts at 94.53% lines, 78.68% branches, and 95.44% functions. The current gate exposes only Node's three metrics and asserts that line coverage equals statement coverage; it also excludes scripts/ from the source walk. The implementation tranche must add an independently reported statements threshold, retain fail-closed all-source presence checks, cover real behavioral/error paths, and prove negative controls before this item can close."
  "2026-08-07T14:46:33.183Z","harness:codex","2026-08-07 completion evidence: the fail-closed gate now measures index.ts,docstrings.ts,coverage-gate.ts,docstring-gate.ts,and prepare-merge-driver.ts. The suite runs 162 tests (160 pass and 2 explicitly opt-in real-fleet skips) and c8 reports exact 100% statements,branches,functions,and lines for every required source. Behavioral negative controls prove missing config,invalid source declarations,absent or incomplete lcov,non-zero or unlaunchable runners,all four independent thresholds,and executable ignore entries fail closed."
files[3]{path,scope,note}:
  scripts/coverage-gate.ts,project,Fail-closed four-metric coverage enforcement
  test/coverage-gate.test.ts,project,Coverage gate positive and negative controls
  scripts/prepare-merge-driver.ts,project,Typed cross-platform install hook
tests[1]{command,path,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  npm run coverage,package.json,project,600
close_reason: Exact all-source coverage and anti-bypass acceptance criteria are verified.
